## IOC VALIDATION

Before accepting an IOC:

- Validate its syntax.
- Normalize case where appropriate.
- Remove surrounding punctuation introduced by article formatting.
- Defang/refang indicators correctly.
- Remove duplicates.
- Recognize the same IOC reported by multiple sources.
- Track every source that reported the IOC.
- Exclude RFC1918 addresses.
- Exclude loopback addresses.
- Exclude documentation/example addresses.
- Exclude obvious placeholders.
- Exclude `example.com` style demonstration domains.
- Do not classify a legitimate shared cloud service as malicious merely because a threat temporarily abused it.
- Be very cautious with CDN addresses, cloud provider IPs, URL shorteners, GitHub, Dropbox, OneDrive, Google Drive, AWS, Azure, Cloudflare, Discord CDN, Telegram infrastructure, and other shared infrastructure.
- Clearly label shared infrastructure instead of blindly treating it as malicious.
- Detect sinkholed or retired infrastructure when that information is available.
- Record IOC first-seen and last-seen dates when available.

Every IOC must retain provenance.

